course: dictionary
lesson: 8637
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same letters can mean different things. The word se can be a short form for a direction, a part of a postcode, or a small French word. Context tells you which one it is. «The wind came from the SE.» Here SE is a direction, so it stands for south-east.
explain: Check the clues around it. A map, compass or weather report points to a direction. A French sentence with a verb points to the French word. «Il se lave» means he washes himself, and se is the small word that goes with the verb.
explain: Capital letters help too. SE with capitals is usually an abbreviation in English, such as the south-east or the postcode SE1. Lowercase se in a French or Spanish sentence is a grammar word, not an English word.
fact: SE is short for south-east, the direction halfway between south and east.
fact: SE is also the start of London postcodes, such as SE1.
fact: In French, «se» means himself, herself, itself or themselves, and it sounds like suh.
fact: «Se souvenir» means to remember, so «se» is part of a verb in French.
fact: Spanish has a similar small word, se, but it is not an English word.
exercise: «The wind came from the SE, so the boat sailed north-west.» What does SE stand for? | *south-east | north-east | south-west | Sunny Exit
exercise: «Il se lave» is French. What does it mean? | they wash their hands | he washes the car | he is very tired | *he washes himself
exercise: Roots ending in d, de, se or nd usually take -sion, as in «tense, tension». Which root usually takes -sion? | cook | *tense | jump | happy
test: «She lives in SE1, in London.» Where is SE1? | *south-east London | south-west Scotland | the middle of Paris | north Wales
test: «Elle se souvient» uses the French word «se souvenir», which means what? | to sing | to forget | to sleep | *to remember
exam: You see «se» in a French sentence next to a verb. What should you do? | Skip it, because it never matters | Translate it as the English word see | *Use the context to check that it means himself or herself | Read it as south-east
